# Hillman Imp two-door saloon, 1963-1976.
#
# Rootes' rear-engined small car, built at Linwood: 3,581 mm long, 1,524 mm wide,
# 1,384 mm high, 2,083 mm wheelbase; 875 cc aluminium overhead-cam engine, coil
# spring suspension. The Imp and its derivatives ran to 1976.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillman_Imp
#
# Colours: Ermine White, Island Blue, Cherry Red and Alpine Green are documented
# Rootes colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 120 in total (white 40, blue 32, red 28, green 20).
#
# Speed 130 km/h; comfort 55/413 (line). Classes 1,2.
# Dates: 1963-1976 with a road tail to about 1986.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/hillman-imp.blend. References:
# citycars/references/hillman-imp/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
